Z||000002||AkursedX||06-18-2001||11:18 PM||||Once again, I had a great time this week.  Hehe, and I had a nice little run on my ride home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Hit 115mph on my way home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Gotta love those canadian highways.<P>I can't wait to see the pics! And hopefully I'll post a couple by myself.<P>Oh yeah, Grinthock, you're car is FAST!  You pulled right away from me after we left Tim Hortons, I was impressed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Well hopefully we can get more people out next week!||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||06-18-2001||11:22 PM||||Pics are READY!!! HERE THEY ARE!!<P>8 cars came this week YAY!!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000539.JPG"> <BR>----------------------<BR>The GREEN MACHINE -- 84 T-Top Fully modified<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000542.JPG"> <P>----------------------<BR>Joe from buffalo came up, nice rims!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000543.JPG"> <BR>---------------<BR>This is one of our members who has a cool rain cover for his sunroof, installs real quick, keeps the bird crap out<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000545.JPG"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||06-18-2001||11:22 PM||||------------------<BR>BanditBalz and one of our local 84 Coupe guys, bandit's tellin him how it REALLY works<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000547.JPG">  <BR>-------------------<BR>Ken and his "Green Machine"<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000548.JPG">  <BR>---------------------<BR>Bob - he has a 88GT (behind) sitting in front of my 87GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000549.JPG">  <BR>----------------------<BR>This is our show co-ordinator from the Stoney Creek Optimist club, they are the wonderful people who run the show and give us free stuff!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000551.JPG">  <BR>--------------------<BR>BanditBalz even did a DEMO For everyone, how to do the Brighter Blub upgrade on your PONTIAC lights.  One question, how many Fiero nuts does it take to screw in a lightbulb anyway!!!   In the Black that's Joe (AkursedX!), in the white Fiero Shirt thats BanditBalz, and of course the fat guy is Me!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/S_P000553.JPG">  <BR>-------------<BR><p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 06-18-2001).]||||reg||1
